{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3070","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3070","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3070\",\"parent_revision\":\"8c788546feb04e9a8f53c82fcb2b88b23d39e1451ca2a193f7e14e94b2ae1ede\",\"root_revision\":\"8c788546feb04e9a8f53c82fcb2b88b23d39e1451ca2a193f7e14e94b2ae1ede\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Confirm `/reload-plugins` against the corrected marketplace path actually advances the cached `dh` plugin version and picks up current `work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` content.\\n- [ ] Confirm whether the blank-line-separated `<gate_token>` fix actually resolves the bang-exec failure (test was never completed \u2014 this issue exists because it couldn't be verified in the original session).\\n- [ ] `/dh:work-backlog-item create -- \\\"...\\\"` succeeds end-to-end without the `command not found: ...` error.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a developer, I want `/dh:work-backlog-item` (and any other `dh:` skill invocation) to actually run, so I can use the backlog workflow instead of hitting `Shell command failed for pattern \\\"!`...`\\\": [stderr] (eval):1: command not found: ...` on every invocation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRelated: #2992 (closed) fixed a *different* bug in the same gate-token line \u2014 a `permission denied: ../..` shell-injection issue. This issue's `command not found: ...` symptom is confirmed distinct (CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT resolves correctly for the `dh` plugin generally \u2014 verified via the working sibling skill `dh:dh-meta-docs` \u2014 and the gate-token script itself runs cleanly standalone with the resolved path).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause Found This Session 2026 08 20\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo compounding issues:\\n\\n1. **Stale marketplace source.** `~/.claude/settings.json`'s `extraKnownMarketplaces.jamie-bitflight-skills.source.path` pointed at a deleted worktree (`/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/astral-plugin-adoption`) \u2014 almost certainly left over from an earlier session's temporary test that was never reverted. Fixed in this session by repointing it at `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills` (the root, matching every other \\\"trusted repo\\\" reference already in that settings file).\\n2. **Session cache never re-syncs.** Confirmed empirically: editing `work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` in a live checkout has zero effect on `Skill()` invocations in the same session \u2014 even leaving the file with completely invalid, non-frontmatter content produced byte-identical output to the original. Skill content is snapshotted at `/reload-plugins` time; the plugin cache (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/dh/`) was observed stuck at version `9.0.21` across multiple `/reload-plugins` runs while the working tree's `plugin.json` was already at `9.0.22` \u2014 reload did not advance the cache to match, even after the marketplace-path fix (not yet re-verified after the path fix \u2014 see below).\\n</div>\\n\\n## What S Still Unverified\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Whether reloading against the corrected marketplace path (`~/repos/claude_skills`, not this session's `~/Developer/claude_skills` checkout) actually resolves the gate-token failure. The `<gate_token>` XML-tag/bang-exec adjacency hypothesis (work-backlog-item is the only SKILL.md in the repo with a bang-exec immediately adjacent to a custom XML tag, no blank line) was tested as a fix (commit adding blank-line separation) but never confirmed against a fresh, correctly-sourced reload \u2014 testing was blocked by the stale marketplace path described above.\\n- Whether `~/repos/claude_skills` (a separate checkout from where this session's work happened, `~/Developer/claude_skills`) has the gate-token fix commit at all \u2014 it may be on a different branch/state entirely.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7a503fb34e47191e71a821c04b742835c7c186fe1bfdbf67ba4d123adaaf5d31\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcN8g\"}"}